Subject: base-files: keep uci state and generated configuration in RAM when /var persists

CONFIG_TARGET_ROOTFS_PERSIST_VAR makes /var a directory on the overlay
and links only /var/run into /tmp. OpenWrt's scripts expect /var/state
and /var/etc to start empty on every boot as well: uci keeps interface
state under /var/state, services write their generated configuration
under /var/etc, and nothing clears either. Link both into /tmp too, and
create /tmp/etc at boot; procd creates /tmp/state.

Start9 downstream patch (start-technologies projects/start-wrt).
Applies to: openwrt v25.12.6

--- a/package/base-files/Makefile
+++ b/package/base-files/Makefile
@@ -225,6 +225,8 @@
 else
 	mkdir -p $(1)/var
 	$(LN) /tmp/run $(1)/var/run
+	$(LN) /tmp/state $(1)/var/state
+	$(LN) /tmp/etc $(1)/var/etc
 endif
 	$(LN) /tmp/resolv.conf /tmp/TZ /tmp/localtime $(1)/etc/
 
--- a/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/boot
+++ b/package/base-files/files/etc/init.d/boot
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 	ln -s /var/run /run
 	ln -s /var/lock /run/lock
 	mkdir -p /var/state
+	mkdir -p /tmp/etc
 	mkdir -p /var/tmp
 	mkdir -p /tmp/.uci
 	chmod 0700 /tmp/.uci
